+/*
+(ShaderEmu: files read ahead. A pak's file FS_ReadFile reads has its neighbours in the pak of the same folder and
+extension inflated on workers with nothing to do (sys_shaderemu.cpp's SE_FileGive), each into memory of malloc's: the
+sounds of a character's folder are asked for one at a time, each 170 thousand instructions of zlib's on this core
+(docs/games/jk2.md, "Files read ahead"). FS_ReadFile copies a file read ahead into its buffer when it is asked for in
+that pak, waiting for it if it is not through; one never asked for is let go when the room is wanted, or its pak is.
+A file is read ahead once (se_seen), only while no other file of its pak is open on the pak's own handle, and only
+deflated where it lies in a mapped pak. A pak's folders are not together in it: its entries are chained by their folder
+(se_seen, made at the pak's first read). A folder is read ahead when two files of it with that extension are read one
+after the other (the sounds of a character's table: one of a character's lines, a file a folder of hundreds, is not),
+and what was read ahead of another folder is then let go. What is read ahead lies in one room of 512 KB (se_arena), and
+what is kept of one pak (the first read, of up to 32,768 files) in static arrays: memory of malloc's taken and let go
+a file at a time, or kept, left the machine without an MMU no 10 MB in one piece for the animations' file (a mapping
