+#ifdef SHADEREMU
+// ---- the players made ahead (docs/games/jk2.md, "The players on workers"; se_slot.h)
+// Before the entities' loop, every player of the snapshot (ET_PLAYER: the player and the NPCs, a tenth of a million
+// instructions each a frame of play, their Ghoul2 bones and bolts, shadows and angles) is made by CG_AddCEntity on a
+// worker core of its own (or on this one, when none is free), what it asks of the engine recorded (cl_cgame.cpp); then
+// the loop makes every entity in its turn, a player made ahead by replaying what it recorded. So the engine is asked
+// the same things in the same order as when each is made in its turn, and what a player reads of the others is as it
+// was in its turn: of a player before it the new (it waits for that player: a "wave" after it), of one after it the
+// frame before's (copied first: CG_SE_LookPoint), and a look target that is not a player is placed first. A player that
+// asks what cannot be recorded ends its job (SE_SlotAbort), is put back as it was and is made in its turn, and so is
+// any player waiting on it. A player draws its random numbers from a state of its own (cg_rand.c), in its turn too.
+// JK2_PLAYERS=core: as before, every entity in its turn; =inline: ahead, all on this core. JK2_PLAYERS_LOG=N: a line
+// every N frames (made ahead, by workers, ended and why).
